      "writtenOn": "2024-07-12T16:40:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for your thoughts on this, I didn\u0027t investigate what it would take to keep the LinkedList instead of the vector so it\u0027s good to discuss it. There\u0027s a lot of historical reasons why we had both linked lists and vectors, and TBH I don\u0027t remember all of them exactly. The current set of things we need to do is:\n\n - Manage (ID, generation) to reuse them when possible, incrementing the generation.\n - Loop over all the objects to unregister or cancel callbacks on them.\n - From an ID, generation, retrieve the object.\n \nRetrieving the object needs a Map\u003cID, Object\u003e which is a vector. However typing this I wondered where it is used, and it\u0027s just for `HandleDeviceLoggingCallback` and `HandleDeviceUncapturedErrorCallback` which would both disappear with futures. (although the logging callback doesn\u0027t have a replacement for now).\n\nWith all this discussion I\u0027m thinking we can keep the vector in the ObjectStore. We can always change our minds later and add back the LinkedList but moving to just WireIDManager (aka ObjectStore without vector) and a LinkedList would require a bunch more work right now.",
